  "content": {
    "id": "v2-6f6da7410-practice-slot-11-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": null,
    "prompt": "The curve $y=x^3+ax^2-9x+2$ has a stationary point at $x=3$.\nFind the value of $a$ and the coordinates of the other stationary point.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$a=-3$; the other stationary point is $(-1,7)$.",
      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}y'&=3x^2+2ax-9\\\\y'(3)&=27+6a-9=0\\\\6a&=-18\\\\a&=-3\\end{align*}$$\nThen $y=x^3-3x^2-9x+2$ and\n$$\\begin{align*}y'&=3x^2-6x-9\\\\&=3(x-3)(x+1)\\end{align*}$$\nThe other stationary point has $x=-1$.\n$$\\begin{align*}y(-1)&=(-1)^3-3(-1)^2-9(-1)+2\\\\&=7\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": null
  },
